  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1200 AM CDT Mon Jun 22 2026\n\nHot and dry conditions will prevail across the area Tuesday\nthrough the rest of the week and into the upcoming weekend.\nA strong upper level ridge will be centered over the Desert \nSouthwest and extend eastward across Texas this week. By the\nend of the week, the ridge will flatten out across the area,\nas a large upper trough develops across the western states. \nThis pattern will result in hot and dry conditions across West\nCentral Texas, with above normal temperatures through the \nperiod.\n\nThrough mid week, temperatures will be hot but will likely stay \nbelow heat advisory criteria, with highs ranging from the mid 90s \nsouth, to low 100's (100 to 104 degrees) across portions of the \nConcho Valley and Big Country. Temperatures are expected to \nincrease further towards the end of the week and into the weekend,\nwith highs in the upper 90s along the I-10 corridor and triple \ndigits elsewhere. At this time it appears that heat related \nproducts are likely for portions of the area beyond Thursday.",
